# Local Identity development overrides (ticket #57, spec #8).
#
# Copy to `.env` (ignored by Git; never commit real secrets) and start the
# Worker with `npm run dev:local` (`wrangler dev --env-file .env`). Every
# `AUTH_*` name below matches the canonical runtime variable name used by
# the versioned environment profiles in `src/config/profiles.ts`, so a
# same-name value here overrides the selected profile without translation.
# Sandbox/production secrets are configured directly in Cloudflare and never
# belong in any `.env` file.
#
# Non-secret local overrides (defaults mirror the versioned local profile;
# uncomment and change a value to exercise a different local scenario):
ENVIRONMENT=local
AUTH_REGISTRATION_ENABLED=true
AUTH_EMAIL_PASSWORD_ENABLED=true
AUTH_REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION=true
# AUTH_MAIL_TRANSPORT is unset by default so local development uses the
# metadata-only development mail sink (no credentials, no network delivery).
# Select "resend" or "smtp" for real-delivery acceptance (ticket #58):
# - resend: set RESEND_API_KEY below plus AUTH_MAIL_ALLOWLIST covering the
#   local test address (the non-production allowlist guard also applies to
#   local real delivery).
# - smtp: set SMTP_HOST/SMTP_PORT/SMTP_SECURE plus SMTP_USER/SMTP_PASSWORD
#   below, e.g. port 587 with SMTP_SECURE=false (STARTTLS) or port 465 with
#   SMTP_SECURE=true (implicit TLS). Port 25 is rejected on Workers. Local
#   SMTP delivery is allowlist-guarded like Resend, so set
#   AUTH_MAIL_ALLOWLIST to cover the local test address.
# AUTH_MAIL_TRANSPORT=
AUTH_MAIL_FROM=User Service <noreply@example.com>
AUTH_APP_NAME=User Service
# AUTH_MAIL_ALLOWLIST is only required where a real transport runs outside
# production; leave it unset for local development.
# AUTH_MAIL_ALLOWLIST=
# SMTP submission configuration (ticket #58, provider-neutral: Gmail, Amazon
# SES SMTP, Exchange or a client-owned SMTP service). Non-secret part; the
# credentials live in the secrets section below.
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=
# SMTP_SECURE=
#
# Consumer token configuration (spec #150). Local/test runs use
# deterministic local-only issuer/audience/TTL defaults, so these slots stay
# commented for ordinary development. Uncomment to exercise explicit values;
# sandbox/production fail closed without explicit issuer/audience.
# AUTH_JWT_ISSUER=
# AUTH_JWT_AUDIENCE=
# AUTH_JWT_TTL_SECONDS=900
# AUTH_GATEWAY_ORIGINS=
# Direct-browser consumer origins (spec #164, ADR-0013): exact http(s)
# origins granted credentialed CORS on the consumer identity operations and
# accepted for cookie-auth mutations. Empty means same-origin-only. Example
# for local real separate-origin acceptance:
# AUTH_CONSUMER_ORIGINS=http://localhost:4321
#
# Local secrets (empty slots only; fill them in `.env`, never here):
# - BETTER_AUTH_SECRET: optional locally (falls back to a documented
#   dev-only value); required in sandbox/production via `wrangler secret`.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# - RESEND_API_KEY: only needed locally if AUTH_MAIL_TRANSPORT=resend is
#   selected for real-delivery acceptance.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# - SMTP_USER / SMTP_PASSWORD: only needed locally if
#   AUTH_MAIL_TRANSPORT=smtp is selected for real-delivery acceptance.
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
